 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a>
 
 The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
 
+The directory is served in two forms: the paged HTML page and a machine-readable form carrying the same veterinarians, the latter reinstated as a supported surface `[REQ-VET-003]`. Either form can be narrowed to only the veterinarians holding a named specialty. The name is matched in full — not as a prefix — and letter case does not distinguish it. The HTML page paginates the narrowed list, and its pagination links carry the named specialty so a narrowed result stays navigable across pages `[REQ-VET-003]`. A named specialty that no veterinarian holds narrows the list to nothing — a normal, successful page or document with no veterinarians, not a failure. An absent, empty, or whitespace-only name leaves the full directory unchanged, exactly as owner search treats an empty term `[REQ-VET-003]`. The narrowing is requested through the address alone; this round adds no on-page control for it, and a visible control may follow as a separate request.
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that some veterinarians hold, when the HTML page is opened narrowed to that specialty, then only those veterinarians are listed, a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that some veterinarians hold, when the machine-readable form is requested narrowed to that specialty, then only those veterinarians are returned.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty name differing from a held specialty only by letter case, when either form is narrowed to it, then it matches; given a name that is only the beginning of a specialty, when either form is narrowed to it, then it does not match.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a name that no veterinarian's specialty equals, when either form is narrowed to it, then the response is a normal, successful page or document listing no veterinarians.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given an absent, empty, or whitespace-only specialty name, when either form is requested, then the full directory is returned as though no narrowing were asked.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a narrowed HTML result spanning more than one page, when a pagination link is followed, then the narrowing is preserved and the next page shows only matching veterinarians.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. The machine-readable form of the directory is a supported surface as of 2026-08-26 (`REQ-VET-003`); its earlier status as an unrequested artifact is recorded in the Superseded list under the withdrawn `REQ-VET-002`.
 
-**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts) · **ADR:** [ADR: Free-Text Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope; Filtering the Directory by a Displayed Specialty Is In Scope](adr/2026-08-26-non-goal-veterinarian-search.md)
 
